# The town sign, written as a dialogue script (.vn). It becomes the event 'town/sign'.
# Lines: "who: text", "who:pose: text", "> narration", commands, "$ any TypeScript".
# Blocks are indented: choice options (* text) and if / elif / else.
# "title" names the event on saves made during it.

title The town sign

> An old wooden sign. Someone carved a message into it.
> {i}"Welcome to town. Be kind to the slimes."{/i}

if flag('read_sign'):
  > You have read it before. It hasn't changed.
else:
  set read_sign = true
  > Behind the sign, half buried, something glints.
  choice:
    * Dig it up
      give apple
      money +5
      > An apple and a few coins. Lucky!
    * Leave it
      > You leave it where it is.

# A tour of the visual-novel features (src/content/events/town/showcase).
> A note is pinned below: {i}"Engine tour, ask here."{/i}
choice:
  * Take the tour
    event town/showcase
  * Not now
    > Maybe later.
